---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const install =
  'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sovereign-cognitive-identity/sci/main/scripts/install.sh | bash';

const props = [
  {
    title: 'Privacy proxy',
    body: 'Sci runs as a local proxy on your Mac. Before any request reaches Anthropic, it finds your name, email, and other identifiers and swaps them for stable placeholder tokens — then restores them in the reply. The model still does its job; it just never learns who you are.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Persistent memory',
    body: 'A local memory store, exposed to Claude Code over MCP, remembers your projects, preferences, and past decisions. Start a fresh session in a new directory and the context is already there — no re-explaining yourself every morning.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Sovereign by default',
    body: 'Everything lives on your machine: a local SQLite database, embeddings computed on-device, your credentials untouched. Nothing about you is sent to a Sci server — because there is no Sci server.',
  },
];

const steps = [
  { n: '01', t: 'Intercept', d: 'Claude Code’s HTTPS proxy points at sci-helper on port 3001. Every request to Anthropic passes through it first.' },
  { n: '02', t: 'Anonymize', d: 'Sci detects PII and replaces it with placeholder tokens, keeping a local map. The outbound request carries only the tokens.' },
  { n: '03', t: 'Restore', d: 'Anthropic’s reply comes back through Sci, which swaps the tokens for your real values before Claude Code ever sees it.' },
];

const roadmap = [
  {
    phase: 'Shipped',
    label: 'Alpha v0.1.0',
    items: [
      'Claude Code on macOS (Apple Silicon)',
      'PII anonymization for the Anthropic API',
      'Local memory over MCP — recall, store, identity',
    ],
  },
  {
    phase: 'Next',
    label: 'In progress',
    items: [
      'More agents: Cursor, Copilot, and any MCP client, with tiered access',
      'Multi-provider anonymization: OpenAI, OpenRouter, Google',
      'Intel Mac support',
    ],
  },
  {
    phase: 'Later',
    label: 'On the roadmap',
    items: [
      'Menu-bar app and auto-update',
      'Optional encrypted cloud sync — Dropbox, S3, iCloud',
      'Nightly memory consolidation',
      'Linux and Windows',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title="Sci">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="kicker">DancingBits</div>
    <div class="badge">Alpha v0.1.0 · macOS · Apple Silicon</div>
    <h1>Use Claude Code.<br />Keep your identity to yourself.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Sci is a local proxy that sits between Claude Code and Anthropic. It strips your personal
      details out of every request before it leaves your machine, restores them in the reply, and
      gives Claude a private, persistent memory of your work — all without ever holding your credentials.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/install">Install the alpha</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/what-is-sci">Why Sci?</a>
    </div>
    <div class="install-box">
      <span class="prompt">$</span>
      <code>{install}</code>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-foot">No API key to paste. Sci works with the Claude Code login you already use — including Claude Pro &amp; Max via OAuth.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="problem">
    <h2>Every prompt is a disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      The tools that make you faster also see everything you type — your name, your clients, your
      codebase, the half-formed ideas you’d never put in a public repo. That data trains models,
      lands in logs, and crosses networks you don’t control. And the moment a session ends, the
      context you spent an hour building is gone.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sci changes the deal. You keep the speed of Claude Code. The model stops learning who you are,
      and your context stops disappearing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="example">
    <h2>See it in one request</h2>
    <div class="ba">
      <div class="ba-col">
        <div class="ba-label">You type</div>
        <pre><code>Hi, I'm Casey Zandbergen
(casey@dancingbits.ai).
Review the auth flow for
my startup's login page.</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="ba-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="ba-col">
        <div class="ba-label out">What reaches Anthropic</div>
        <pre><code>Hi, I'm [PERSON_1]
([EMAIL_1]).
Review the auth flow for
my startup's login page.</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ba-note">The reply comes back with <code>[PERSON_1]</code> restored to your name — so the conversation reads naturally on your end, while the model only ever saw the tokens. Run <code>sci verify</code> after install to watch it happen live.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="props">
    {props.map((p) => (
      <div class="prop">
        <h3>{p.title}</h3>
        <p>{p.body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="steps-sec">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      {steps.map((s) => (
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-n">{s.n}</div>
          <div>
            <h3>{s.t}</h3>
            <p>{s.d}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p>Meanwhile a local agent backs Claude’s memory tools over MCP, reading and writing to an on-device store. <a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works">See the full architecture →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="trust">
    <h3>Sci never holds your keys</h3>
    <p>
      The proxy is transparent: it forwards whatever credentials Claude Code already sends — your
      OAuth session or your own API key — without storing or inspecting them. There’s no account to
      create and no key to hand over. Your data and your credentials stay on your machine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="roadmap-sec">
    <h2>Where it's going</h2>
    <p class="roadmap-intro">The alpha is deliberately narrow — one tool, done well. Here's the path from there. The foundations for what's next already live in the codebase.</p>
    <div class="roadmap">
      {roadmap.map((col) => (
        <div class={`rm-col rm-${col.phase.toLowerCase()}`}>
          <div class="rm-head">
            <span class="rm-phase">{col.phase}</span>
            <span class="rm-label">{col.label}</span>
          </div>
          <ul>
            {col.items.map((it) => <li>{it}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta">
    <h2>Try the alpha</h2>
    <p>One command on an Apple Silicon Mac. About three minutes, start to finish.</p>
    <div class="install-box">
      <span class="prompt">$</span>
      <code>{install}</code>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:18px">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/install">Install guide</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/what-to-test">What to test</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    section { margin-bottom: 64px; }
    .hero { padding: 56px 0 8px; max-width: 840px; }
    .kicker { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      color: var(--accent); background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
      border-radius: 999px; padding: 5px 14px; margin-bottom: 22px;
    }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 48px; line-height: 1.08; font-weight: 800; color: #f8fafc; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: 20px; }
    .lede { font-size: 19px; color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 28px; max-width: 660px; }
    .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .btn { display: inline-block; padding: 11px 22px; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; text-decoration: none; transition: all 0.15s; }
    .btn.primary { background: var(--accent-strong); color: #04263a; }
    .btn.primary:hover { background: var(--accent); }
    .btn.ghost { color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border-accent); }
    .btn.ghost:hover { background: var(--panel-2); }
    .install-box { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; overflow-x: auto; }
    .install-box .prompt { color: var(--green); font-family: "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace; }
    .install-box code { background: none; color: #93c5fd; padding: 0; font-size: 13px; white-space: nowrap; }
    .hero-foot { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 12px; }

    h2 { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; color: #f1f5f9; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 16px; }
    .problem, .example, .steps-sec, .trust, .final-cta { max-width: 760px; }
    .problem p { font-size: 16.5px; color: #cbd5e1; margin-bottom: 14px; }

    .ba { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 14px; align-items: center; }
    .ba-label { font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 700; }
    .ba-label.out { color: var(--green); }
    .ba-col pre { margin: 0; }
    .ba-col code { white-space: pre; }
    .ba-arrow { color: var(--accent); font-size: 22px; }
    .ba-note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 16px; }

    .props { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 18px; max-width: none; }
    .prop { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px; }
    .prop h3 { font-size: 16px; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .prop p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim); }

    .steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .step { display: flex; gap: 16px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px; }
    .step-n { font-family: "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); padding-top: 2px; }
    .step h3 { font-size: 16px; color: #f1f5f9; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .step p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text-dim); }
    .steps-sec > p { font-size: 15px; color: #cbd5e1; }
    .text-link { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
    .text-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    .trust { background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--border-accent); border-radius: 14px; padding: 26px 28px; }
    .trust h3 { font-size: 18px; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .trust p { font-size: 15.5px; color: #cbd5e1; }

    .final-cta p { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 18px; }

    .roadmap-sec { max-width: none; }
    .roadmap-intro { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
    .roadmap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 18px; }
    .rm-col { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 22px; }
    .rm-col.rm-shipped { border-color: #14532d; }
    .rm-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 14px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .rm-phase { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 800; color: #f1f5f9; }
    .rm-shipped .rm-phase { color: var(--green); }
    .rm-label { font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; }
    .rm-col ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    .rm-col li { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim); padding: 6px 0 6px 18px; position: relative; }
    .rm-col li::before { content: '→'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--accent); }
    .rm-shipped li::before { content: '✓'; color: var(--green); }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .hero h1 { font-size: 33px; }
      .props { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .ba { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .ba-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); justify-self: center; }
      .roadmap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
